KG42.register("rules-6c6584a51dc3d6956ec7eaf3",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R010","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Microgrids capable of supplying locally generated energy may participate in the DNEM. Scope: Microgrid participation in the DNEM within the proposed hierarchical electricity market. Direct participation of microgrids in the WEM is not applicable. Scope: Direct microgrid participation in the WEM, distinct from participation through the hierarchical market arrangement.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Direct microgrid participation in the WEM, distinct from participation through the hierarchical market arrangement. | Microgrid participation in the DNEM within the proposed hierarchical electricity market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E008"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Microgrids capable of supplying locally generated energy may participate in the DNEM. Scope: Microgrid participation in the DNEM within the proposed hierarchical electricity market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E001","v141-b-g01-E008"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Direct participation of microgrids in the WEM is not applicable. Scope: Direct microgrid participation in the WEM, distinct from participation through the hierarchical market arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"Abstract This paper proposed a hierarchical structure for the electricity market to facilitate the c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"In the proposed hierarchical structure, microgrids participate in the energy market at the distribution networks settled by the distribution network operator (DNO), and load aggregators (LAs) interact with microgrids and generation companies (GENCOs) to import/export energy to/from the distribution network electricity markets from/to the wholesale electricity market. The proposed approach addressed the synergy of energy markets by introducing dynamic game with complete information for GENCOs, microgrids, and LAs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p02-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"RUCTURE FOR THE SMART GRID PARADIGM 1867 he respective bidding strategies. Direct participation of m","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Direct participation of microgrids in the WEM is not applicable for the following reasons: 1) technical limitations on voltage levels, generation, and demand capacity; 2) lack of an efficient business model and technical infrastructure to provide microgrids with access to open access same-time information system and open access nondiscriminatory transmission services; 3) shortage in an efficient framework to evaluate the potential services provided by microgrids in the WEM; and 4) increase in the number of microgrids, with diverse capacities and coverage areas; and the technical restraints on transmitting electricity to the bulk power network including congestion and voltage constraints [16], [17]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-B Microgrids Objective","anchor_text":"ds ψ′ ≤ψ′j ≤ψ′j (2) jme- he ρ′j = ψ′j 2αjPje + βj ; Pje = Pj. (3) nd e on B. Microgrids Objective de","equation_id":"(4)-(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Microgrid m maximizes the payoff function (4), subjected to the limitations on the bidding vector as shown in (5). Here, the first term in the payoff function is the revenue of the microgrid and the second term is the generation cost. The generation dispatch of microgrids is provided by curtailing the IL and dispatching the DERs. The microgrid may adopt several policies to serve its demand. One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM while the other is to bid on its total generation capacity in the DNEM and serve the local demand economically from the distribution network. In both cases, the bidding vector for generation in microgrid m is shown in (6)\nR_m = \\max_{P_m,\\psi_m} \\left[ \\lambda_0 \\cdot P_m - \\left(\\alpha_m P_m^2 + \\beta_m P_m + \\gamma_m\\right) \\right] \\tag{4}\n\\underline{\\psi}_m \\le \\psi_m \\le \\bar{\\psi}_m \\tag{5}\n\\rho_m = \\psi_m(2\\alpha_m P_{me} + \\beta_m); \\quad \\sum_e P_{me} = P_m. \\tag{6}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The rule is a qualitative participation/admission rule. The C.1 graph and the supplied source text define no design-selection or operational decision variable for participation.prosumer; C001 and C002 are permission/exclusion statements, not optimization variables or dispatch decisions.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule defines no fixed parameter, coefficient, bound, or constant for participation.prosumer. The source evidence identifies market scope and participant type, but supplies no numeric or symbolic parameter for this admission rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E001","quote":"In the proposed hierarchical structure, microgrids participate in the energy market at the distribution networks settled by the distribution network operator (DNO)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","quote":"The microgrid may adopt several policies to serve its demand. One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","quote":"Direct participation of microgrids in the WEM is not applicable"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"0d5f157b9373186a45383c7d389aef5292c0d3d3be0371d6740e1b4aa6032b5c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule contains only qualitative participation/admission statements: microgrids may participate in the DNEM, and direct microgrid participation in the WEM is not applicable. The supplied source text and C.1 graph declare no decision variable, parameter, equation, inequality, optimization condition, or equilibrium condition for participation.prosumer; V contains only participation.prosumer and E is empty. This is therefore a procedural/admission rule rather than a mathematical one, and no expression is invented.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a unary DNEM participation permission for microgrids. Its only approved graph member is participation.prosumer. The frozen graph has no edge for this procedural permission, so no edge is cited. Evidence v141-b-g01-E001 states that microgrids participate in the DNO-settled distribution-network energy market, and v141-b-g01-E008 states that a microgrid may bid excess generation in the DNEM."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is a unary exclusion of direct microgrid participation in the WEM. Its only approved graph member is participation.prosumer. The frozen graph has no edge representing this exclusion, so no edge is cited. Evidence v141-b-g01-E003 states that direct participation of microgrids in the WEM is not applicable."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
